// Level up — ONE synth, deep, a single sustained harmony. No ladder, no arrival
// note, no second voice.
//
// It has been three things now. A two-chord sawtooth cadence with a bell was
// "stately", which is the one thing this game is not. A three-note triangle rise
// fixed the register but was still a MELODY, and a melody competes with the
// music for attention at the exact moment the game pauses. This is a chord: it
// lands, it sits, it gets out of the way.
//
// Deep on purpose. The whole sfx palette was pulled down after the 2026-08-02
// playtest ("too many sounds and all too similar"), and low is the one register
// nothing else in the game occupies — the level-up cue can own it outright.
//
// Root, fifth, octave. No third, because the gameplay tracks rotate through
// A Aeolian, D Phrygian and A Dorian, and a third is wrong over two of them.
note("[a2,e3,a3]").s("triangle")
  .attack(.012).decay(.55).sustain(0)
  .lpf(1700).gain(.8)
